The compiler wrapper starts from the project's GPL-2.0-only A618 canonical
producer and host prototype. Mesa is built from unchanged pinned compiler
sources, with the explicit platform/build edits in build.py and port.py.
Mesa source copyright and license notices are preserved in the private overlay.
Most Mesa compiler components use the MIT license; consult the pinned source.

Scarlet C runtime platform code and cross/audit tooling are adapted from the
MIT-licensed sgfx-shader-agx implementation in scarlet-project-applesilicon;
that checkout is read-only and not modified by this crate.

The glass.wgsl test fixture is copied from ScarletUI's actual SGFX glass shader
for regression coverage (blur_vertex, glass_vertex, horizontal, vertical, glass,
erase). It is test input, never a replacement for caller shader source.

The private printf adapter builds LLVM libc printf_core from the SDK-pinned
LLVM source, licensed Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception. Upstream copyright and
license headers remain in those source inputs; no prebuilt printf is used.
